4", "owner": "kagami.pnw", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18261084415287687, "text": "コレ最高😃💕欲しい💖💖💖🐉🍀‼️", "created_at": "2025-02-28T19:13:44", "owner": "gingro_zasshonokumanojo", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18001319447746452, "text": "Top😍", "created_at": "2025-02-28T15:23:54", "owner": "___annina86___", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18053794483908410, "text": "😮😮😮❤️❤️❤️❤️", "created_at": "2025-02-27T15:51:24", "owner": "suhrobbek_8903", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18491264320043733, "text": "Romantizar", "created_at": "2025-02-27T03:13:28", "owner": "gaboo_prime", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17924874975020610, "text": "ai que calor só de assistir", "created_at": "2025-02-23T10:16:12", "owner": "dulcesimoun", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18067245301850299, "text": "Can I buy this similar car . I m from India", "created_at": "2025-02-22T10:48:44", "owner": "anikadabra", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18005199200548991, "text": "Ở đâu tôi có thể mua cái này?", "created_at": "2025-02-21T23:29:46", "owner": "miranda_makes_beauty", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17885141199218232, "text": "Ok ! But we would like to see the rest of the car 🙌 😉", "created_at": "2025-02-21T16:30:50", "owner": "sergiobna", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18147083707367839, "text": "😍😍", "created_at": "2025-02-20T21:31:59", "owner": "rayla_viviane", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18082595671539049, "text": "Hello", "created_at": "2025-02-20T17:14:37", "owner": "anuragsingh1983", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17937522086978023, "text": "❤️❤️", "created_at": "2025-02-20T15:51:55", "owner": "akshdeep2005", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17960120768900895, "text": "I want to buy a she your Car", "created_at": "2025-02-19T16:11:11", "owner": "akamsssa.rbs", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18089935024497009, "text": "@bydautobrasil", "created_at": "2025-02-19T13:48:37", "owner": "conectafigures", "likes": 0}], "location": null, "hashtags": []},
{"media_id": 3485521997172384288, "shortcode": "DBfD8oSRSIg", "permalink": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DBfD8oSRSIg/", "taken_at": "2024-10-23T23:39:47", "caption": "don’t let me get bored #roblox #physics", "owner_username": "circdev.98", "owner_id": "53911013759", "likes": 12491, "is_video": true, "typename": "GraphVideo", "media": [{"type": "video", "path": "0353_DBfD8oSRSIg\\DBfD8oSRSIg_20241023_233947.mp4"}], "comments": [{"id": 18023337698444122, "text": "That’s one way to spend 45 minutes to solve a 10 minute problem😂. All of the cool points were earned, though!  Now make a code for Desmos to let you freely switch graph axes like LoggerPro", "created_at": "2024-10-24T00:43:46", "owner": "chuktuttle", "likes": 1072}, {"id": 18116543593431082, "text": "Answer is 7.5 m/s² 🔥", "created_at": "2025-01-23T22:14:48", "owner": "adelbazzine", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17959806245849372, "text": "just use euler-lagrange 😭😭😭", "created_at": "2025-01-07T12:57:40", "owner": "fauzanadhiimaa", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18054807733992621, "text": "Then you remember you have to show the steps", "created_at": "2025-01-06T09:11:14", "owner": "kagtama", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18479177497020171, "text": "Jesus loves you and wants you to get to talk to him and pray and read your Bible ❤️", "created_at": "2025-01-04T16:33:00", "owner": "thenonmusicppl", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17971445777803750, "text": "4.11m/s2", "created_at": "2024-12-14T09:57:37", "owner": "keyan.prv", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18329583223155815, "text": "🔥", "created_at": "2024-12-11T14:48:03", "owner": "ethan.y152", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18086141806481991, "text": "12.9m/s^2", "created_at": "2024-12-07T15:29:16", "owner": "arjun.bhatt1", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18039324584337052, "text": "Bro used physics to solve physics", "created_at": "2024-11-30T15:52:30", "owner": "briaan._____", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18058985017850746, "text": "4.1m/s^2", "created_at": "2024-11-28T16:55:51", "owner": "cessbeckham", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18382334014097454, "text": "bro use the more harder way💀", "created_at": "2024-11-28T10:39:59", "owner": "tjl_chen", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18100080688464021, "text": "The immense power of procrastination.", "created_at": "2024-11-27T21:44:52", "owner": "kramarova_tereza", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18078124135601974, "text": "custom physical properties = true, adjust density until you get your desired mass", "created_at": "2024-11-26T16:33:42", "owner": "kubek_kuba2", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18474768322034556, "text": "(g-4)/sqrt(2) ≈ 4.106 m/s²", "created_at": "2024-11-23T23:17:24", "owner": "punjabilol1988", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18049617305507149, "text": "bro just write the lagrangian and x = xrel + xcm", "created_at": "2024-11-23T18:50:55", "owner": "max_mogadam", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18049369483846414, "text": "2.128 m/s^2 i took g = 10 m/s^2 for easier calculation", "created_at": "2024-11-23T13:23:13", "owner": "neonexe_error", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17875154655216773, "text": "Just solve the problem bro 😭🙏😭🙏", "created_at": "2024-11-23T06:30:09", "owner": "mattia_t16", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18046713713086209, "text": "Calculated and seems that the box stays still and the ramp somehow goes 167kj/football feild in the z direction at a angle pi/3i", "created_at": "2024-11-23T04:10:45", "owner": "sebastian_a66", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17951309048856790, "text": "Project the 4 accleration onto the plane, project the 9.81 acceleration due to gravity on to the plank and the net acceleration is their sum", "created_at": "2024-11-20T18:31:15", "owner": "k.evin_zzz", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18033104990108314, "text": "Bro did ALL THAT just to mess it up by putting m/s² instead of ms‐²", "created_at": "2024-11-17T17:34:37", "owner": "oskar.zp1", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17843240796349462, "text": "Why not just learn the actual physics?", "created_at": "2024-11-10T23:42:23", "owner": "solemisalomi", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18012131522648393, "text": "Bro can get a 4 on ap comp sci A but not do the freest kinematic question 😭", "created_at": "2024-11-09T08:15:11", "owner": "jofthevant", "likes": 6}, {"id": 18022888709277011, "text": "approximately 9.75 m/s²", "created_at": "2024-11-06T01:12:58", "owner": "carlos.penterich", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18043263541934743, "text": "Due to 45 deg angle there's symmetry between horizontal and vertical forces, so fnet = m (g-a)/sqrt(2)", "created_at": "2024-11-05T16:17:24", "owner": "jakcbu", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17884617144137790, "text": "Working harder and harder", "created_at": "2024-11-02T20:33:42", "owner": "erzincanliposer", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18047380976021235, "text": "2.08 m/s^2 ☝️🤓", "created_at": "2024-11-01T20:11:02", "owner": "fefito_tweak", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18100626925456141, "text": "just write a lagrangian for the system and solve euler lagrage equations smh", "created_at": "2024-10-31T09:29:36", "owner": "max02.fortnite.pl", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17944202273875881, "text": "9.76 m/s^2?", "created_at": "2024-10-31T04:54:41", "owner": "elijah_valdiviax", "likes": 4}, {"id": 17908978128030620, "text": "you dont even need the mass for it no?", "created_at": "2024-10-31T00:37:35", "owner": "el_plato_del_perro", "likes": 6}, {"id": 18097351540466172, "text": "2.9 m/s^2 there’s a pseudo inertial force you need to account for", "created_at": "2024-10-30T21:56:41", "owner": "iamsnake_big_boss", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18469947484000964, "text": "I got about ~6m/s². Ax = 4m/s², and since it's a 45 triangle, Ay = Ax. The block's acceleration is going downwards due to gravity (assume 10m/s²). Subtract: g - Ay = 6m/s²", "created_at": "2024-10-30T13:13:35", "owner": "ronnyy_mo", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18035260148262826, "text": "you actually solve the equation though", "created_at": "2024-10-29T04:54:37", "owner": "jung_eraname", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18097115878463439, "text": "just solve analytically lil bro", "created_at": "2024-10-28T22:51:34", "owner": "charlieismsm", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18346145665122926, "text": "lmfao", "created_at": "2024-10-28T01:23:59", "owner": "_notrajiv", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18080530936489309, "text": "Don't watch at night. You will experience POV Foxy fnaf 2", "created_at": "2024-10-28T00:21:11", "owner": "aaron_kimball_", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18372443842111002, "text": "i think it's going at 8,905 m/s - may be wrong though.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T19:10:23", "owner": "fareast613", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18044118020316022, "text": "How old are you brother please dont tell me we are the same age", "created_at": "2024-10-26T18:25:28", "owner": "hno.sk", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17929469570848405, "text": "pls do t80 autoloader, i will love you forever", "created_at": "2024-10-26T16:14:08", "owner": "m2browningtracerrounds", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18045256568047104, "text": "pls dobt", "created_at": "2024-10-26T16:13:55", "owner": "m2browningtracerrounds", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18204522721289203, "text": "i want to learn how to do this", "created_at": "2024-10-25T17:04:21", "owner": "jerrydtp", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18362882425115046, "text": "8,m/s² there", "created_at": "2024-10-25T04:22:07", "owner": "www_sp3nser_com", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18055886059883634, "text": "Nigga...", "created_at": "2024-10-25T03:22:52", "owner": "panzerfaustas", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17957537519712181, "text": "It’s obviously -9.81 m/s^2 lol", "created_at": "2024-10-25T01:39:33", "owner": "kawaii_bunnyhunter", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18136220599365543, "text": "Is that a Minecraft Block?", "created_at": "2024-10-24T17:38:00", "owner": "redaceone", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18061814332777034, "text": "i got about 4.108m/sec sq", "created_at": "2024-10-24T16:36:05", "owner": "nhansp._", "likes": 6}, {"id": 18036574403010485, "text": "I am using scrap mechanic", "created_at": "2024-10-24T16:19:43", "owner": "fatihkartal64", "likes": 3}, {"id": 17886281367109274, "text": "thats... actually a highschool level problem... how is it hard?", "created_at": "2024-10-24T14:31:56", "owner": "thisguyoninstaisme", "likes": 69}, {"id": 17929671341841125, "text": "Keyboard is Corsair k70. Ok mid-range. My only problem with it are the cheap key caps that wore off in half a year of osu!ania.", "created_at": "2024-10-24T13:47:48", "owner": "benjaminsetow", "likes": 102}, {"id": 17897365353148648, "text": "😂I can do all this on the paper", "created_at": "2024-10-24T13:37:47", "owner": "sutharsiddhant", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18155687896323196, "text": "@circdev.98 bouta be the next Albert Einstein 🔥", "created_at": "2024-10-24T08:07:06", "owner": "emilis.art", "likes": 2}, {"id": 17884636251137311, "text": "To solve the problem, let's break it down.\nProblem Summary:\nA wedge with a 45-degree angle is moving on a frictionless surface with an acceleration of .\nA block of mass  slides down the wedge without friction.\nWe are asked to find the acceleration of the block relative to the ground.\nSolution:\nWe have a 2D problem where:\nThe wedge is accelerating horizontally with .\nThe block moves along the inclined plane, which means its acceleration is influenced both by gravity and the wedge's motion.\nStep 1: Set the coordinate system\nAssume a non-inertial frame attached to the wedge.\nThe block experiences two accelerations: one due to gravity along the incline and another due to the wedge's acceleration.\nStep 2: Analyze the forces on the block\nIn the wedge's frame, the block feels the following:\n1. A component of gravitational force pulling it down the incline:  where  and .\n2. The horizontal acceleration of the wedge affects the block. From the block's perspective, the wedge accelerates horizontally to the left with , creating an inertial force acting horizontally.\nStep 3: Equations of motion\nFor the block's acceleration down the incline:\nGravitational acceleration component along the incline: .\nFor the acceleration of the wedge affecting the block:\nThe horizontal component of the block's acceleration is influenced by the wedge’s motion:\na_{block_x} = a - g \\sin(45^\\circ) = 4 - 6.93 \\ \\text{m/s}^2.\nI'll compute this step next.\n7.53m per second sq.", "created_at": "2024-10-24T06:01:17", "owner": "kolodziejczyk_antnek", "likes": 18}, {"id": 18055194091881630, "text": "i used roblox as desmos cause i didnt know how to use desmos lmao", "created_at": "2024-10-24T04:50:45", "owner": "th3ltgrounds", "likes": 7}, {"id": 18270084871300370, "text": "Bro working harder AND smarter.", "created_at": "2024-10-24T03:23:03", "owner": "math.sousa456", "likes": 36}, {"id": 18468014146025060, "text": "is that 2d kinematics", "created_at": "2024-10-24T02:46:40", "owner": "nathangcmag", "likes": 8}, {"id": 18039849827321400, "text": "Tuff", "created_at": "2024-10-24T01:38:28", "owner": "mase_maher", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18061467877701164, "text": "Amazing bro 👍", "created_at": "2024-10-24T01:00:48", "owner": "b_impossible_d", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17956623911832798, "text": "It’s frictionless, so the only forces acting on the block are gravity (mg) acting at -90 degrees, and the normal force acting at +45 degrees from horizontal. I believe the normal force will be mg(root2)+m(4/root2)m/s^2, being the sum of the reaction of a block sliding down an unaccelerated ramp plus the normal component of the 4m/s^2 acceleration of the ramp itself. Adding these two forces together and dividing by mass (which actually doesn’t impact the result), I get acceleration components of Ax=11.8m/s^2 and Ay=+2m/s^2, indicating that the ramp will in fact push the block up and over itself. Combining the components I get an an absolute acceleration of 11.97m/s at +9.59 degrees from horizontal. \n\nThis all assuming they want the absolute acceleration, rather than relative acceleration along the ramp in the ramp’s 4 m/s^2 accelerated reference frame.", "created_at": "2024-10-24T00:51:33", "owner": "geoffrey_machin", "likes": 89}, {"id": 17925290993970582, "text": "\" Work harder not smarter \" lol but very talented for even bothering to do this", "created_at": "2024-10-24T00:29:11", "owner": "yves72_", "likes": 376}, {"id": 18043202153286761, "text": "Bro, you don't need to be doing all that lol", "created_at": "2024-10-24T00:00:05", "owner": "thepepsimanishere", "likes": 123}, {"id": 17941210784909443, "text": "we love circuit!!!!", "created_at": "2024-10-23T23:42:47", "owner": "maxx_acco", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18472233046051519, "text": "It asks for acceleration man are you stupid", "created_at": "2024-11-19T06:25:09", "owner": "t.savovv", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18045388583020578, "text": "Dude, it’s like- movement in an accelerated frame of reference, you simply add a force pointing left equal to maR’/R…\nMy dude opened fcking Roblox studio, ggs :’)", "created_at": "2024-11-03T09:45:33", "owner": "melk_dml", "likes": 0}], "location": null, "hashtags": ["roblox", "physics"]},
